#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105471 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9846ca00-8305-56a8-a14d-7aa2488c0016" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Exterior Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "0cd03b60-baf3-5689-9f84-5f8be9853a9b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12838" :question/problem "Consider the hexagon shown below. Draw an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](images/fc/fc1834e88b4d08a2705059d28d21105047898f251f0f2c29f8509be7b6321de0.png)" :question/worked-solution "To construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B,$ we extend $\\overline{AB}$ past $B.$ The angle between $\\overline{BC}$ and the extension of $\\overline{AB}$ is an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](images/d9/d91fc772042490e0785a4a617e4c3785c8616b7ed0ff05509ca8bc902eccc2a8.png)\n\nAnother way to construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B$ is to extend $\\overline{CB}$ past $B.$ The angle between $\\overline{AB}$ and the extension of $\\overline{CB}$ is also an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](images/8d/8d031a6a6cc1513fc0a8031755b537d144279b88c964fc75728d3588ae1e4af9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105472 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5de9bf2f-b11c-5af0-a569-5f25aebae227" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Exterior Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "fbc903e6-45ee-53c5-9d31-0edf8140cacd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12839" :question/problem "![](images/02/02ac83b8318d6067ba7959c390ccb8b011001ebcb289e4f31c27ba8e1ceb2913.png)\n\nIn the figure above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle{F}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $\\angle F.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{100}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{78}^{∘}+{62}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {300}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={360}^{∘}-{300}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "44ea9915-91ca-5abf-a1ac-bb801069ef24" :question/math-academy-id "e-12879" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f2d7f92335d965840f8714dc4ceeb43201ecee2ada9b7aeb7eb54437a0f7d0f.png)\n\nFind the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $A$ is $180^\\circ - 90^\\circ=90^\\circ$ and the measure of the exterior angle at $D$ is $180^\\circ - 2x.$ \n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ},$  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{90}^{∘}+(x+{10}^{∘})+({180}^{∘}-2x)+x+(x+{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{290}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/id #uuid "e96a16e9-122f-582c-beb9-22ca0d4d7d68" :question/math-academy-id "e-12880" :question/problem "![](images/22/22130cbd3bb1f36d9ef8ce6290eead15354bbced7810e5fad5ac62972cd1d968.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle A.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(12x-{5}^{∘})+(6x+{5}^{∘})+(10x)+(9x-{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 37x-{10}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 37x & ={360}^{∘}+{10}^{∘} \\\\ 37x & ={370}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-{5}^{∘} & =12({10}^{∘})-{5}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}-{5}^{∘} \\\\  & ={115}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9846ca00-8305-56a8-a14d-7aa2488c0016" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac84abb-e41e-5560-b12c-9bac37afdb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b3/b36ad546ab0fc8c6cc87ce6d9e2b8262250915dcca208bcc06bcd694c75f0336.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505933} {:answer/id #uuid "81e6cf21-1f6c-5f64-b267-f5d06cbfe716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/36e26991e3514fe1027c9cd0a139e3349b3a84106d3986c01e2292f247a415bd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506134} {:answer/id #uuid "da84c738-0514-52d6-9d50-aa04b9c586f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec2b11d02a5db393be9d9841b4b19ffeaed0e8eaf9b1be6ef057ab9be6fab467.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506302} {:answer/id #uuid "eef6ce64-de26-598c-ac8f-f953b1e77621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/460dfbcaa6cf9f4158d5e9cb5e3f01d53c13fb56b4aa06833da4b03bde0fbcfc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506350} {:answer/id #uuid "fa03f032-30c3-5d56-9aff-5f41b0233862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c882240065e7e3da6a5a8b9797a471fa793dd25d350f5d058a94d1be66a80dd2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da84c738-0514-52d6-9d50-aa04b9c586f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec2b11d02a5db393be9d9841b4b19ffeaed0e8eaf9b1be6ef057ab9be6fab467.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506302} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c81f7da-823a-5028-b9d6-eabbccda4172" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41756a29-a06c-5e68-84f6-73d196f1e63f" :question/math-academy-id "q-118214" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f6ccd25845b1b21e5ae9ecb3b05380313e1db71cb1c773c06c49db57d6b724e0.png)\n\nConsider the pentagon shown above. Which of the following shows an exterior angle of $∠E?$" :question/worked-solution "To construct an exterior angle of $∠E,$ we extend $\\overset{―}{DE}$ past $E.$ The angle between $\\overset{―}{AE}$ and the extension of $\\overset{―}{DE}$ is an exterior angle of $∠E.$\n\n![](images/ec/ec2b11d02a5db393be9d9841b4b19ffeaed0e8eaf9b1be6ef057ab9be6fab467.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5de9bf2f-b11c-5af0-a569-5f25aebae227" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245ac979-94fb-5171-b340-7516865a9645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505970} {:answer/id #uuid "2d576976-a264-5b3a-aa68-547e49962124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505991} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f71e9c-187f-5acd-9a12-64bdf15d2462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506216} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb0174b-9c86-52c0-9e7a-2ff0a0239db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506229} {:answer/id #uuid "e159b985-c6ab-5b86-bca4-a0604a5721e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d576976-a264-5b3a-aa68-547e49962124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505991} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d3483b2-0cc2-5606-83de-5d1597fb33b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae89a7d0-62b6-55ff-a90b-0514ff252b15" :question/math-academy-id "q-118357" :question/problem "![](images/62/6252354d464db3c645186b9a8ef6001ee76408b04f7abf6a9046656270607085.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let us call $z$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{50}^{∘}+z+{80}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{100}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {280}^{∘}+z & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0956c0d-2efe-5ef7-923e-90941b8f2e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0956c0d-2efe-5ef7-923e-90941b8f2e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506200} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a24cec-e3bb-5524-a269-d61c5cfa2b21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a62fde9-6a09-5998-9eb3-129787e83051" :question/math-academy-id "q-223196" :question/problem "![](images/40/409b89d99c494f3273ce228ebb828e440a3c5ab4940344e775680225eed84d8b.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+(x+{40}^{∘})+(3x-{40}^{∘})+3x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 9x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ad3649-c78e-5b83-b0f1-c3b2b5cc427e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506007} {:answer/id #uuid "41a4a9df-6823-5440-9387-1d9555aa339f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{98}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506022} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0a8c65-746c-5068-9c13-fbbadc1ed3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506036} {:answer/id #uuid "a61c3dfc-f5dc-56b4-98d9-a4c8a9519960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{102}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506214} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2705c8-1eb8-5d43-ad6c-71362d85e87b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{95}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b0a8c65-746c-5068-9c13-fbbadc1ed3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506036} :answer-field/id #uuid "f63f6de2-8f84-5c1b-88a7-4d31118f7fa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88db253f-f4d0-5a45-9c21-b523cf1fc7e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-223263" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e07e30d981b25aefa18192e38408516423072dcd84e2352bc962df3888c41a04.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $D$ is ${180}^{∘}-(6x+{4}^{∘})={176}^{∘}-6x.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9x-{17}^{∘})+(5x-{5}^{∘})+4x+({176}^{∘}-6x)+(3x+{11}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (9x+5x+4x-6x+3x)+(-{17}^{∘}-{5}^{∘}+{176}^{∘}+{11}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 15x+{165}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 15x & ={195}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={13}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-{17}^{∘} & =9({13}^{∘})-{17}^{∘} \\\\  & ={117}^{∘}-{17}^{∘} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9846ca00-8305-56a8-a14d-7aa2488c0016" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a8f7cf2-b4ad-51d5-8e94-a4c47e2692b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4a4aeff749a6272032f69cdf1631daf352fe9ab601f549d255751107a1f4e0b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506092} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4b81c9-ba73-5390-bc8e-8f718fde1729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3bd1be72d6189ec3b3b2f7ead34be4d95f534db8a31b46a1d3989778e3cae1e1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506095} {:answer/id #uuid "b17b940b-06c6-595e-9916-a618e505eb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.t