ligned}{41}^{∘}+{106}^{∘}+{127}^{∘}+z & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {274}^{∘}+z & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={86}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "281e10bb-1ae7-56d7-a26b-9e8aa699a6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{53}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505979} {:answer/id #uuid "382b07e6-3ec6-5b8a-957e-bbdfe8a69d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506006} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2091c8-a2f6-5e8b-88c7-5e3d7ba50c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506040} {:answer/id #uuid "bde2f157-7b2c-5eca-82d7-cdecf946c8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506253} {:answer/id #uuid "dec57432-f09d-5d34-90ed-7265e888dca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382b07e6-3ec6-5b8a-957e-bbdfe8a69d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506006} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1958022-8300-50ad-9317-2aae7f708e69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bd80e8d-878b-5ffb-88fb-5a3f8d18232d" :question/math-academy-id "q-68128" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b98ac3a59b0726c47d273b06891f9aeabcb0b31c9e5937887464fec0205cb677.png)\n\nFind the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(x-{8}^{∘})+(2x+{4}^{∘})+(2x-{14}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x-{18}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={378}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={63}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d78c07-0074-5c61-ad9f-15cb9fa4bc7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{53}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505927} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8179f8-7c80-5afc-b348-1ee744151b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505992} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbf1ef1-2900-52be-85be-fb6bf9f5cb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506071} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3c9eb3-21b9-5e17-8373-46790271e175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506182} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ecbfb9-f75b-5c87-90a2-1055bbd237bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{43}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bbf1ef1-2900-52be-85be-fb6bf9f5cb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506071} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd0eab80-2a37-5438-acfe-dd7442b0e7d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38b881c5-6a5a-5455-82f5-12615cde9f7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79418" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac5d02edc0945574b5bf8f9a1112e9d7e9ca33ebc7714bfadcd14d02e46c43c7.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $C$ is ${180}^{∘}-(4x-{1}^{∘})={181}^{∘}-4x,$ and the measure of the exterior angle at $E$ is ${180}^{∘}-{86}^{∘}={94}^{∘}.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+{1}^{∘})+(2x+{14}^{∘})+({181}^{∘}-4x)+(2x+{16}^{∘})+{94}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (2x+2x-4x+2x)+({1}^{∘}+{14}^{∘}+{181}^{∘}+{16}^{∘}+{94}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 2x+{306}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={54}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={27}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{1}^{∘} & =2({27}^{∘})+{1}^{∘} \\\\  & ={55}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
